## Background
Came up hard. Most bandits in Skyrim were ordinary people once — failed farmers, dismissed soldiers, runaway thralls, impoverished sons and daughters who couldn't make an honest coin in the Hold's harsh trade. Drifted into a gang because gangs eat. Bounty in two or three Holds, depending on how active they've been. No safe city to walk into without risking the dungeon. Lives in the wilderness on the rotation between temporary camps and a permanent hideout — until the next adventurer or guard patrol pushes them out and they have to find another.
